;;; macro.xtm -- a polyphonic macro-oscillator: six synthesis engines from Plaits

;; Author: Ben Swift
;; Keywords: extempore

;;; Commentary:

;; A port of six of the synthesis engines in Mutable Instruments Plaits, a
;; Eurorack "macro-oscillator" designed by Emilie Gillet. Plaits packs many
;; different ways of making a sound behind the same three knobs: HARMONICS,
;; TIMBRE and MORPH. What each knob does depends on the engine, but the idea is
;; always the same: harmonics picks the raw material, timbre brightens it, and
;; morph changes its character.
;;
;; The `engine` parameter picks one:
;;
;;   0 va --- virtual analogue. OUT is a variable saw (morph: triangle, notched
;;     saw, saw, then fading out) plus a variable square (timbre: off, thin
;;     pulse, square, then hard-synced to a sweeping slave). Harmonics detunes
;;     the saw: 0.5 is unison, and either side steps through a fifth, an
;;     octave, an octave and a fifth and two octaves, down or up. AUX is a
;;     "monster sync" pair: two detuned variable-shape oscillators, each synced
;;     to the note, with timbre setting how far above the note they run.
;;   1 fold --- waveshaping. A variable-slope triangle (morph: its asymmetry)
;;     goes through a waveshaper (harmonics: from a soft inverse-tangent curve
;;     at 0.0, through linear at 0.5, to bumpy curves at 1.0) and then a sine
;;     wavefolder (timbre: how hard it's driven), at twice the sample rate on
;;     notes above about 265 Hz. AUX is a triangle turned into a sine and
;;     crossfaded, by timbre, into a model of the Buchla 259's wavefolder.
;;   2 fm --- two-operator FM, computed at four times the sample rate.
;;     Harmonics picks the frequency ratio of modulator to carrier, from a list
;;     of musically useful ones (0.5, 0.71, 1, 1.41, 2, 3, pi, 4 and so on,
;;     with a few slightly detuned ones in between). Timbre is the modulation
;;     index, which is eased back on high notes and high ratios so that the
;;     sidebands stay below the Nyquist frequency. Morph is feedback: above 0.5 the carrier modulates the
;;     modulator's phase (towards noise), below 0.5 its frequency (towards
;;     chaos). AUX is a sine an octave below, modulated by the carrier.
;;   3 grain --- formant synthesis. Each cycle of the note fires a short burst
;;     (a "grainlet") of a sine at a formant frequency, so the note keeps its
;;     pitch while timbre sweeps the formant from 33 Hz to 4 kHz. Two grainlets
;;     are summed: harmonics sets the interval between their formants (two
;;     octaves down to two up) and, below 0.5, lets some of the bare pulse
;;     through. Morph shapes the burst's window. AUX is a "Z" oscillator, a
;;     windowed sine reset twice a cycle, similar to the Casio CZ's resonant
;;     waveforms: timbre is its resonant frequency, morph its window and
;;     harmonics the shape of the reset.
;;   4 harmonic --- additive. Twenty-four harmonics, with a spectral peak at a
;;     position set by timbre, a width set by morph (narrow at 0.0, wide at
;;     1.0) and harmonics adding ripples (bumps) across the spectrum. AUX uses
;;     the same envelope over the harmonics of a Hammond's drawbars (1, 2, 3,
;;     4, 6, 8, 10 and 12).
;;   5 swarm --- eight sawtooth waves (and eight sines on AUX), spread in pitch
;;     by harmonics. Each wanders in grains: timbre is how often they move and
;;     morph how long each grain lasts, from a cloud of glissandi at 1.0 to
;;     short, separate grains at 0.0. As on Plaits when it's triggered, each
;;     note starts with a burst of fast movement which then settles.
;;
;; Plaits shapes its oscillator with a low-pass gate: a filter and an
;; amplifier which open and close together, the way a vactrol (a lamp shining
;; on a light-dependent resistor) does in a Buchla LPG. A note "pings" the
;; vactrol open in about half a cycle, and it then closes with a quick initial
;; drop and a slow tail. As it closes, the filter's cutoff falls from 14 kHz
;; towards 150 Hz, which is what gives Plaits its plucked, woody notes.
;; `colour` sets how much it behaves as a filter (0.0: all of the sound goes
;; through the closing filter) or as an amplifier (1.0: the highs bleed past
;; it), and `decay` sets how long it rings. Velocity sets how far the ping
;; opens the vactrol, so softer notes are both quieter and darker.
;;
;; The same note also starts a decay envelope, which Plaits can route to timbre
;; and morph: `timbre-env` and `morph-env` set how far it moves each one, up
;; or down.
;;
;; Plaits is a percussive instrument at heart: its low-pass gate always
;; closes. Two things here let it hold a note too. `sustain` is a level the
;; vactrol is held at while the key is down (0.0 is Plaits' own pluck, 1.0
;; keeps it wide open), and an ordinary attack and release envelope follows the
;; gate after it.
;;
;; Every engine has two outputs, OUT and AUX, which are often quite different
;; sounds. `aux` crossfades between them, and `width` spreads them apart: with
;; aux at 0.5 and width at 1.0, OUT is on the left and AUX on the right.
;;
;; How the code is laid out. Plaits renders in blocks of 12 or 24 samples:
;; once per block it turns the knobs into oscillator settings (frequencies,
;; pulse widths, gains), and within the block each setting glides in a
;; straight line to its new value, so that turning a knob doesn't make zipper
;; noise. The studio calls a voice once per frame instead, so each engine here
;; is a closure which is called with a `ctl` flag: MACRO_BLOCK_START on the
;; first frame of each 24-frame block, when it works out its new targets and
;; aims a ramp at each, and MACRO_SAMPLE on the frames in between, when it
;; steps the ramps and renders one sample. MACRO_NOTE_START is a block start
;; on which the ramps jump straight to their targets, and MACRO_NOTE_RESET is
;; the same with the phases of the oscillators whose relative phase shapes the
;; sound (the virtual analogue and FM engines) set back to their starting
;; values, so that a note sounds the same whatever the voice played before.
;;
;; Harmonics, timbre and morph glide towards their settings with a time
;; constant of 10 ms, so that a stepped `ctl` doesn't click. A note which
;; starts on a voice that is still sounding fades the old one out over 5 ms
;; and then starts, so that a stolen voice doesn't click. A new note's DC
;; blockers start as a running mean, which removes the offset of a pulse wave
;; within a few periods instead of the 30 ms a fixed 5 Hz highpass takes.
;;
;; Plaits works in normalised frequency (cycles per sample, at 48 kHz) and
;; reads its pitch, sine and shaper curves from tables. Here frequencies are
;; worked out from SRf, so the tuning is right at any sample rate, and the few
;; tables which remain (a sine, the waveshaper curves and the FM ratios) are
;; computed from the same formulas Plaits' table generator uses, when this file
;; loads. Plaits' rate constants which are tied to its 4 kHz block rate (the
;; envelope speeds) are scaled by the block length in seconds. There are six
;; voices. The chord,
;; wavetable, speech, noise, physical-modelling and drum engines aren't here.
;;
;; This is a port of code from Mutable Instruments Plaits
;; (https://github.com/pichenettes/eurorack, plaits/dsp and stmlib/dsp),
;; which carries this notice:
;;
;;   Copyright 2016 Emilie Gillet.
;;
;;   Author: Emilie Gillet (emilie.o.gillet@gmail.com)
;;
;;   Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a
;;   copy of this software and associated documentation files (the
;;   "Software"), to deal in the Software without restriction, including
;;   without limitation the rights to use, copy, modify, merge, publish,
;;   distribute, sublicense, and/or sell copies of the Software, and to permit
;;   persons to whom the Software is furnished to do so, subject to the
;;   following conditions:
;;
;;   The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included
;;   in all copies or substantial portions of the Software.
;;
;;   THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS
;;   OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF
;;   MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN
;;   NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM,
;;   DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR
;;   OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE
;;   USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.

;;; Code:

(sys:load-preload-check 'studio-macro)
(define *xtmlib-studio-macro-loaded* #t)

(sys:load "libs/studio/api.xtm")

(def-instrument macro
  "a macro-oscillator: six synthesis engines from Mutable Instruments Plaits"
  (params
    (engine 0.0 "synthesis engine: 0 va, 1 fold, 2 fm, 3 grain, 4 harmonic, 5 swarm")
    (harmonics 0.52 "the engine's first macro control, 0.0 to 1.0 (see the commentary)")
    (timbre 0.35 "the engine's second macro control, usually brightness, 0.0 to 1.0")
    (morph 0.45 "the engine's third macro control, usually character, 0.0 to 1.0")
    (timbre-env 0.0 "how far the decay envelope moves timbre, -1.0 to 1.0")
    (morph-env 0.0 "how far the decay envelope moves morph, -1.0 to 1.0")
    (decay 0.55 "how long the low-pass gate and decay envelope ring, 0.0 (short) to 1.0 (long)")
    (colour 0.4 "low-pass gate response: 0.0 is a filter, 1.0 an amplifier")
    (sustain 0.6 "how open the low-pass gate stays while a note is held, 0.0 to 1.0")
    (attack 0.002 "seconds to fade in")
    (release 0.25 "seconds to fade out after the note ends")
    (aux 0.0 "the balance of the OUT and AUX outputs, 0.0 (OUT) to 1.0 (AUX)")
    (width 0.0 "how far OUT and AUX are spread to the left and right, 0.0 to 1.0")
    (level 0.8 "output level"))
  (presets
    (poly (level 0.72))
    (pluck (harmonics 0.5) (timbre 0.55) (morph 0.5) (sustain 0.0) (decay 0.6)
           (colour 0.1) (timbre-env 0.4))
    (sync (timbre 0.6) (morph 0.55) (timbre-env 0.5) (decay 0.5) (sustain 0.7)
          (aux 0.5) (width 0.8) (release 0.15))
    (folded (engine 1.0) (harmonics 0.35) (timbre 0.25) (morph 0.5) (timbre-env 0.6)
            (decay 0.5) (sustain 0.2) (colour 0.3) (aux 0.3) (width 0.5) (level 1.1))
    (epiano (engine 2.0) (harmonics 0.35) (timbre 0.2) (morph 0.5) (timbre-env 0.45)
            (decay 0.7) (sustain 0.25) (colour 0.6) (aux 0.4) (width 0.6) (release 0.4)
            (level 0.78))
    (bell (engine 2.0) (harmonics 0.82) (timbre 0.35) (morph 0.5) (timbre-env 0.3)
          (decay 0.85) (sustain 0.0) (colour 0.8) (aux 0.15) (width 0.6) (release 1.5)
          (level 0.86))
    (vowel (engine 3.0) (harmonics 0.62) (timbre 0.4) (morph 0.3)
           (sustain 0.8) (colour 0.7) (aux 0.0) (attack 0.03) (release 0.3) (level 0.85))
    (organ (engine 4.0) (harmonics 0.0) (timbre 0.3) (morph 0.85) (sustain 1.0)
           (colour 0.9) (aux 1.0) (attack 0.005) (release 0.08)
           (level 0.5))
    (glass (engine 4.0) (harmonics 0.45) (timbre 0.55) (morph 0.35) (timbre-env 0.3)
           (decay 0.8) (sustain 0.35) (colour 0.7) (aux 0.4) (width 0.8) (release 0.8)
           (level 1.17))
    (swarm (engine 5.0) (harmonics 0.28) (timbre 0.6) (morph 0.8) (sustain 1.0)
           (colour 0.6) (aux 0.4) (width 1.0) (attack 0.4) (release 1.2) (level 0.78))))

;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
;; small building blocks ;;
;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;

;; the number of frames in a control block (Plaits uses 12 or 24)
(bind-val MACRO_BLOCK i64 24)

;; what an engine is asked to do on this frame
(bind-val MACRO_SAMPLE i64 0)      ;; render one sample
(bind-val MACRO_BLOCK_START i64 1) ;; take new settings, then render
(bind-val MACRO_NOTE_START i64 2)  ;; the same, jumping to them at once
(bind-val MACRO_NOTE_RESET i64 3)  ;; the same, and the oscillators restart their phases

;; Above this f0 (cycles per sample, about 265 Hz at 44.1 kHz) the waveshaping
;; engine runs at twice the sample rate and comes back down through the kit's
;; halfband filter, which keeps the harmonics the shaper and folder add from
;; folding into the audible band as hard.
(bind-val MACRO_OS_F SAMPLE 0.006)

;; an engine: (ctl f0 harmonics timbre morph out) renders one frame, writing
;; OUT to out[0] and AUX to out[1]. f0 is the note's frequency in cycles per
;; sample; harmonics, timbre and morph are read only when ctl isn't MACRO_SAMPLE.
(bind-alias MacroEngine [void,i64,SAMPLE,SAMPLE,SAMPLE,SAMPLE,SAMPLE*]*)

(bind-macro "x limited to lo..hi, as a SAMPLE" (macro_clamp x lo hi)
  `(let ((clamp_x:SAMPLE ,x) (clamp_lo:SAMPLE ,lo) (clamp_hi:SAMPLE ,hi))
     (if (< clamp_x clamp_lo) clamp_lo (if (> clamp_x clamp_hi) clamp_hi clamp_x))))

;; The helpers used on every sample (ramps, polyBLEPs, the sine) are macros
;; rather than functions, so that they're compiled inline: each call to
;; another bind-func costs a few nanoseconds, and an engine makes dozens of
;; them a frame.

;; A ramp glides a setting from its current value to a new target over one
;; block (Plaits' ParameterInterpolator). 0 value, 1 increment per frame.
(bind-type MacroRamp <SAMPLE,SAMPLE> (printer? . #f))

(bind-func static macro_ramp_to
  "aim the ramp at target, arriving in MACRO_BLOCK frames, or at once if jump"
  (lambda (r:MacroRamp* target:SAMPLE jump:i1)
    (if jump
        (begin (tset! r 0 target) (tset! r 1 0.0) void)
        (begin (tset! r 1 (/ (- target (tref r 0)) (convert MACRO_BLOCK SAMPLE))) void))))

(bind-macro
  "step the ramp r on by one frame and return its value"
  (macro_ramp r)
  `(let ((macro_ramp_ptr ,r)
         (macro_ramp_x (+ (tref macro_ramp_ptr 0) (tref macro_ramp_ptr 1))))
     (tset! macro_ramp_ptr 0 macro_ramp_x)
     macro_ramp_x))

(bind-func static macro_ramp_make
  (lambda (n:i64)
    (let ((r:MacroRamp* (zalloc n))
          (i:i64 0))
      (dotimes (i n) (tfill! (pref-ptr r i) 0.0 0.0))
      r)))

;; polyBLEP corrections (stmlib/dsp/polyblep.h). An oscillator which jumps by
;; one at fraction t of the way through a sample adds (this t) to the current
;; sample and (next t) to the following one, which rounds off the step so
;; that it doesn't alias. The integrated versions do the same for a sudden
;; change of slope. t must lie in 0.0 to 1.0: outside it the polynomials grow
;; without bound, and a sudden change of pulse width (a new note on a reused
;; voice) can put an edge behind the phase, so the oscillators clamp it.
(bind-macro "polyBLEP: the correction to this sample" (macro_blep_this t)
  `(let ((blep_t ,t)) (* 0.5 blep_t blep_t)))
(bind-macro "polyBLEP: the correction to the next sample" (macro_blep_next t)
  `(let ((blep_u (- 1.0 ,t))) (* -0.5 blep_u blep_u)))
(bind-macro "integrated polyBLEP: the correction to the next sample" (macro_iblep_next t)
  `(let ((iblep_t1 (* 0.5 ,t)) (iblep_t2 (* iblep_t1 iblep_t1)))
     (- (+ 0.1875 (* 1.5 iblep_t2)) (+ iblep_t1 (* iblep_t2 iblep_t2)))))
(bind-macro "integrated polyBLEP: the correction to this sample" (macro_iblep_this t)
  `(macro_iblep_next (- 1.0 ,t)))

;;;;;;;;;;;;
;; tables ;;
;;;;;;;;;;;;

;; Each table is built once, when this file loads, from the formula in
;; plaits/resources/lookup_tables.py.

;; one cycle of a sine in 512 steps (two extra points for interpolation)
(bind-func macro_build_sine_table
  (lambda ()
    (let ((t:SAMPLE* (halloc 514))
          (i:i64 0))
      (dotimes (i 514)
        (pset! t i (sin (* STWOPI (/ (convert i SAMPLE) 512.0)))))
      t)))

(bind-val macro_sine_table SAMPLE* (macro_build_sine_table))

(bind-macro
  "sin(2 pi phase), for any phase, from the table (linearly interpolated)"
  (macro_sine phase)
  `(let ((sine_x (* 512.0 ,phase))
         (sine_i:i64 (convert sine_x))
         (sine_whole (if (< sine_x (convert sine_i SAMPLE)) (- sine_i 1) sine_i))
         (sine_frac (- sine_x (convert sine_whole SAMPLE)))
         (sine_j (& sine_whole 511))
         (sine_a (pref macro_sine_table sine_j)))
     (+ sine_a (* sine_frac (- (pref macro_sine_table (+ sine_j 1)) sine_a)))))

;; The waveshaper curves (borrowed by Plaits from Tides). Each is an odd
;; function of its input in -1.0 to 1.0, in 257 steps, and there are five:
;; inverse tangent, inverse sine, linear, a bump and a double bump.
(bind-func static macro_ws_curve
  (lambda (shape:i64 x:double)
    (let ((scale (atan 8.0))
          (arg (- 1.0 (* 2.0 x)))
          (fade (if (< (- 4.0 (* 4.0 x)) 1.0) (- 4.0 (* 4.0 x)) 1.0)))
      (cond ((= shape 0)
             (set! arg (/ (tan (* scale arg)) 8.0))
             (/ (acos (if (> arg 1.0) 1.0 (if (< arg -1.0) -1.0 arg))) 3.141592653589793))
            ((= shape 1) (/ (acos arg) 3.141592653589793))
            ((= shape 2) x)
            ((= shape 3)
             (/ (* (- 1.0 (cos (* 3.141592653589793 x 1.5)))
                   (- 1.0 (cos (* 3.141592653589793 fade))))
                4.5))
            (else (sin (* 3.141592653589793 x 1.5)))))))

(bind-func macro_build_ws_table
  (lambda ()
    (let ((t:SAMPLE* (halloc (* 5 257)))
          (shape:i64 0)
          (i:i64 0)
          (u:double 0.0))
      (dotimes (shape 5)
        (dotimes (i 257)
          (set! u (/ (convert (- i 128) double) 128.0))
          (pset! t (+ (* shape 257) i)
                 (convert (if (< u 0.0)
                              (* -1.0 (macro_ws_curve shape (* -1.0 u)))
                              (macro_ws_curve shape u))
                          SAMPLE))))
      t)))

(bind-val macro_ws_table SAMPLE* (macro_build_ws_table))

;; One stage of the Buchla 259 wavefolder: an inverting amplifier which
;; saturates, mixed back with its input through resistors.
(bind-func static macro_deadband
  (lambda (v_in:double r_in:double r_load:double)
    (let ((r_fb 150000.0)
          (v_sat 10.47)
          (v_out (* (/ (* -1.0 r_fb) r_in) v_in)))
      (if (>= v_out v_sat) (set! v_out v_sat))
      (if (< v_out (* -1.0 v_sat)) (set! v_out (* -1.0 v_sat)))
      (/ (+ (* v_in r_fb r_load) (* v_out r_in r_load))
         (+ (* r_fb r_load) (* r_in r_load) (* r_in r_fb))))))

;; The two wavefolders, each in 516 steps across -1.0 to 1.0. The first
;; (rows 0) is a sine folding many times near the middle and an arctangent
;; further out; the second (row 1) is the 259's five folding stages summed
;; into a soft-clipping diode.
(bind-func macro_build_fold_table
  (lambda ()
    (let ((t:SAMPLE* (halloc (* 2 516)))
          (raw:double* (salloc (* 2 516)))
          (i:i64 0)
          (x:double 0.0)
          (w:double 0.0)
          (v:double 0.0)
          (s45:double 0.0)
          (peak1:double 0.0)
          (peak2:double -1000.0))
      (dotimes (i 516)
        (set! x (- (/ (convert (if (= i 515) 514 i) double) 256.0) 1.0))
        (set! w (exp (* -8.0 x x)))
        (pset! raw i (+ (* w (sin (* 8.0 3.141592653589793 x))) (* (- 1.0 w) (atan (* 3.0 x)))))
        (if (> (fabs (pref raw i)) peak1) (set! peak1 (fabs (pref raw i))))
        (set! v (* 12.0 x))
        (set! s45 (- (+ (* (/ -33.0 71.4) (macro_deadband v 30000.0 71400.0))
                        (* -1.0 (macro_deadband v 68000.0 33000.0)))
                     (* (/ 33.0 240.0) v)))
        (set! v (- (+ (* -1.5 (macro_deadband v 10000.0 100000.0))
                      (* (/ -150.0 44.2) (macro_deadband v 49900.0 44200.0))
                      (* (/ -150.0 18.0) (macro_deadband v 91000.0 18000.0)))
                   (* (/ 150.0 33.0) s45)))
        (pset! raw (+ 516 i) (/ (* 0.7 v) (+ 0.3 (fabs v))))
        (if (> (pref raw (+ 516 i)) peak2) (set! peak2 (pref raw (+ 516 i)))))
      (dotimes (i 516)
        (pset! t i (convert (/ (pref raw i) peak1) SAMPLE))
        (pset! t (+ 516 i) (convert (/ (pref raw (+ 516 i)) peak2) SAMPLE)))
      t)))

(bind-val macro_fold_table SAMPLE* (macro_build_fold_table))

(bind-func static macro_hermite
  "read the table at position index (0.0 to 1.0 spans size steps), with
four-point Hermite interpolation (stmlib's InterpolateHermite)"
  (lambda (table:SAMPLE* index:SAMPLE size:SAMPLE)
    (let ((x (* index size))
          (i:i64 (convert x))
          (f (- x (convert i SAMPLE)))
          (xm1 (pref table (- i 1)))
          (x0 (pref table i))
          (x1 (pref table (+ i 1)))
          (x2 (pref table (+ i 2)))
          (c (* 0.5 (- x1 xm1)))
          (v (- x0 x1))
          (w (+ c v))
          (a (+ w v (* 0.5 (- x2 x0))))
          (b_neg (+ w a)))
      (+ (* (+ (* (- (* a f) b_neg) f) c) f) x0))))

;; The FM engine's modulator/carrier ratios, in semitones. Each of the 23
;; ratios is entered three times, so that the harmonics control has a flat
;; spot on each, and the largest gaps are then split in half until there are
;; 128 steps, with two more copies of the last for interpolation.
(bind-func macro_build_fm_table
  (lambda ()
    (let ((t:SAMPLE* (halloc 130))
          (ratios:SAMPLE* (salloc 23))
          (n:i64 0)
          (i:i64 0)
          (gap:i64 0)
          (widest:SAMPLE 0.0))
      (pfill! ratios 0.5 0.504642 0.707107 0.785398 1.0 1.009285 1.414214 1.570796
              1.75 2.0 2.018570 2.25 2.75 2.828427 3.0 3.141593 3.464102 4.0
              4.242641 4.712389 5.0 5.656854 8.0)
      (dotimes (i 69)
        (pset! t i (* 17.31234 (log (pref ratios (/ i 3))))))
      (set! n 69)
      (while (< n 128)
        (set! widest -1.0)
        (dotimes (i (- n 1))
          (if (> (- (pref t (+ i 1)) (pref t i)) widest)
              (begin (set! widest (- (pref t (+ i 1)) (pref t i))) (set! gap i))))
        (set! i n)
        (while (> i (+ gap 1))
          (pset! t i (pref t (- i 1)))
          (set! i (- i 1)))
        (pset! t (+ gap 1) (* 0.5 (+ (pref t gap) (pref t (+ gap 2)))))
        (set! n (+ n 1)))
      (pset! t 128 (pref t 127))
      (pset! t 129 (pref t 127))
      t)))

(bind-val macro_fm_table SAMPLE* (macro_build_fm_table))

;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
;; oscillators ;;
;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;

(bind-func static macro_varishape_naive
  "the variable-shape waveform at phase p, without any anti-aliasing: a saw
crossfaded to a pulse by square and to a triangle by triangle, both skewed by pw"
  (lambda (p:SAMPLE pw:SAMPLE square:SAMPLE triangle:SAMPLE)
    (let ((saw p)
          (sq (if (< p pw) 0.0 1.0))
          (tri (if (< p pw) (/ p pw) (- 1.0 (/ (- p pw) (- 1.0 pw))))))
      (set! saw (+ saw (* square (- sq saw))))
      (+ saw (* triangle (- tri saw))))))

(bind-func macro_varishape_c
  "Plaits' VariableShapeOscillator, hard-synced to a master oscillator.

The waveshape goes from a triangle (0.0) through a saw (0.5) to a pulse
(1.0), with pw skewing it. Every step and corner is rounded off with
polyBLEPs, including the ones the sync makes. Returns a value in -1.0 to 1.0.

@param master_phase - where the master starts, in cycles; restart returns
the oscillator to that and to the start of its own cycle"
  (lambda (master_phase:SAMPLE)
    (let ((slave_phase:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (next:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (previous_pw:SAMPLE 0.5)
          (high:i1 #f)
          (start_phase:SAMPLE master_phase))
      (lambda (master_f:SAMPLE slave_f:SAMPLE pw_in:SAMPLE waveshape:SAMPLE restart:i1)
        (if restart
            (begin
              (set! master_phase start_phase)
              (set! slave_phase 0.0)
              (set! next 0.0)
              (set! previous_pw 0.5)
              (set! high #f)))
        (let ((mf (if (> master_f 0.25) 0.25 master_f))
              (f (if (> slave_f 0.25) 0.25 slave_f))
              (pw (if (>= f 0.25) 0.5 (macro_clamp pw_in (* 2.0 f) (- 1.0 (* 2.0 f)))))
              (square (* 2.0 (if (> waveshape 0.5) (- waveshape 0.5) 0.0)))
              (triangle (if (< waveshape 0.5) (- 1.0 (* 2.0 waveshape)) 0.0))
              (slope_up (/ 1.0 pw))
              (slope_down (/ 1.0 (- 1.0 pw)))
              (cur next)
              (reset:i1 #f)
              (transition:i1 #f)
              (reset_time:SAMPLE 0.0)
              (p:SAMPLE 0.0)
              (value:SAMPLE 0.0)
              (t:SAMPLE 0.0)
              (step:SAMPLE 0.0)
              (looping:i1 #t))
          (begin
            (set! next 0.0)
            ;; the master wraps: the slave restarts part way through this sample
            (set! master_phase (+ master_phase mf))
            (if (>= master_phase 1.0)
                (begin
                  (set! master_phase (- master_phase 1.0))
                  (set! reset_time (/ master_phase mf))
                  (set! p (+ slave_phase (* (- 1.0 reset_time) f)))
                  (set! reset #t)
                  (if (>= p 1.0) (begin (set! p (- p 1.0)) (set! transition #t)))
                  (if (and (not high) (>= p pw)) (set! transition #t))
                  (set! value (macro_varishape_naive p pw square triangle))
                  (set! cur (- cur (* value (macro_blep_this reset_time))))
                  (set! next (- next (* value (macro_blep_next reset_time))))))
            (set! slave_phase (+ slave_phase f))
            ;; the slave's own edges: up at pw, back down at 1.0
            (set! looping (or transition (not reset)))
            (while looping
              (if (not high)
                  (if (< slave_phase pw)
                      (begin (set! looping #f) void)
                      (begin
                        (set! t (macro_clamp (/ (- slave_phase pw) (+ (- previous_pw pw) f)) 0.0 1.0))
                        (set! step (* triangle (+ slope_up slope_down) f))
                        (set! cur (+ cur (* square (macro_blep_this t))))
                        (set! next (+ next (* square (macro_blep_next t))))
                        (set! cur (- cur (* step (macro_iblep_this t))))
                        (set! next (- next (* step (macro_iblep_next t))))
                        (set! high #t)
                        void)))
              (if (and looping high)
                  (if (< slave_phase 1.0)
                      (begin (set! looping #f) void)
                      (begin
                        (set! slave_phase (- slave_phase 1.0))
                        (set! t (/ slave_phase f))
                        (set! step (* triangle (+ slope_up slope_down) f))
                        (set! cur (- cur (* (- 1.0 triangle) (macro_blep_this t))))
                        (set! next (- next (* (- 1.0 triangle) (macro_blep_next t))))
                        (set! cur (+ cur (* step (macro_iblep_this t))))
                        (set! next (+ next (* step (macro_iblep_next t))))
                        (set! high #f)
                        void))))
            (if reset
                (begin (set! slave_phase (* reset_time f)) (set! high #f)))
            (set! next (+ next (macro_varishape_naive slave_phase pw square triangle)))
            (set! previous_pw pw)
            (- (* 2.0 cur) 1.0)))))))

(bind-func macro_varsaw_c
  "Plaits' VariableSawOscillator: a saw with a notch cut into it at pw
(waveshape 0.0), crossfading to a triangle skewed by pw (waveshape 1.0)."
  (lambda ()
    (let ((phase:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (next:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (previous_pw:SAMPLE 0.5)
          (high:i1 #f)
          (depth:SAMPLE 0.2))
      (lambda (freq:SAMPLE pw_in:SAMPLE waveshape:SAMPLE restart:i1)
        (if restart
            (begin (set! phase 0.0) (set! next 0.0) (set! previous_pw 0.5) (set! high #f)))
        (let ((f (if (> freq 0.25) 0.25 freq))
              (pw (if (>= f 0.25) 0.5 (macro_clamp pw_in (* 2.0 f) (- 1.0 (* 2.0 f)))))
              (triangle waveshape)
              (notch_amount (- 1.0 waveshape))
              (slope_up (/ 1.0 pw))
              (slope_down (/ 1.0 (- 1.0 pw)))
              (step (* triangle (+ slope_up slope_down) f))
              (cur next)
              (notch:SAMPLE 0.0)
              (t:SAMPLE 0.0))
          (set! next 0.0)
          (set! phase (+ phase f))
          (if (and (not high) (>= phase pw))
              (begin
                (set! notch (* notch_amount (+ depth (- 1.0 pw))))
                (set! t (macro_clamp (/ (- phase pw) (+ (- previous_pw pw) f)) 0.0 1.0))
                (set! cur (- (+ cur (* notch (macro_blep_this t))) (* step (macro_iblep_this t))))
                (set! next (- (+ next (* notch (macro_blep_next t))) (* step (macro_iblep_next t))))
                (set! high #t)
                void)
              (if (>= phase 1.0)
                  (begin
                    (set! phase (- phase 1.0))
                    (set! notch (* notch_amount (+ depth 1.0)))
                    (set! t (/ phase f))
                    (set! cur (+ (- cur (* notch (macro_blep_this t))) (* step (macro_iblep_this t))))
                    (set! next (+ (- next (* notch (macro_blep_next t))) (* step (macro_iblep_next t))))
                    (set! high #f)
                    void)))
          (set! next (+ next
                        (* notch_amount (if (< phase pw) phase (+ 1.0 depth)))
                        (* triangle (if (< phase pw)
                                        (* phase slope_up)
                                        (- 1.0 (* (- phase pw) slope_down))))))
          (set! previous_pw pw)
          (/ (- (* 2.0 cur) 1.0) (+ 1.0 depth)))))))

(bind-func macro_slope_c
  "Plaits' Oscillator in its SLOPE shape: a triangle which rises for a
fraction pw of each cycle and falls for the rest, with its corners rounded off."
  (lambda ()
    (let ((phase:SAMPLE 0.5)
          (next:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (high:i1 #t))
      (lambda (freq:SAMPLE pw_in:SAMPLE restart:i1)
        (if restart
            (begin (set! phase 0.5) (set! next 0.0) (set! high #t)))
        (let ((f (macro_clamp freq 0.000001 0.25))
              (pw (macro_clamp pw_in (* 2.0 f) (- 1.0 (* 2.0 f))))
              (slope_up (/ 1.0 pw))
              (slope_down (/ 1.0 (- 1.0 pw)))
              (corner (* (+ slope_up slope_down) f))
              (cur next)
              (t:SAMPLE 0.0))
          (set! next 0.0)
          (set! phase (+ phase f))
          (if (if high (>= phase pw) (< phase pw))
              (begin
                (set! t (macro_clamp (/ (- phase pw) f) 0.0 1.0))
                (set! cur (- cur (* corner (macro_iblep_this t))))
                (set! next (- next (* corner (macro_iblep_next t))))
                (set! high (< phase pw))))
          (if (>= phase 1.0)
              (begin
                (set! phase (- phase 1.0))
                (set! t (/ phase f))
                (set! cur (+ cur (* corner (macro_iblep_this t))))
                (set! next (+ next (* corner (macro_iblep_next t))))
                (set! high #t)))
          (set! next (+ next (if high (* phase slope_up) (- 1.0 (* (- phase pw) slope_down)))))
          (- (* 2.0 cur) 1.0))))))

(bind-func macro_dc_blocker_c
  "a one-pole highpass at cutoff (cycles per sample), as stmlib's OnePole"
  (lambda ()
    (let ((state:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (g:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (old_cutoff:SAMPLE -1.0))
      (lambda (x:SAMPLE cutoff:SAMPLE)
        (if (<> cutoff old_cutoff)
            (begin
              (set! old_cutoff cutoff)
              (set! g (tan (* SPI (macro_clamp cutoff 0.000001 0.45))))))
        (let ((lp (/ (+ (* g x) state) (+ 1.0 g))))
          (set! state (+ (* g (- x lp)) lp))
          (- x lp))))))

;;;;;;;;;;;;;
;; engines ;;
;;;;;;;;;;;;;

;; engine 0: virtual analogue (Plaits' VirtualAnalogEngine, variant 2)

(bind-func static macro_va_interval:[SAMPLE,i64]*
  (lambda (i:i64)
    (cond ((= i 0) 0.0) ((= i 1) 7.01) ((= i 2) 12.01) ((= i 3) 19.01) (else 24.01))))

(bind-func static macro_va_detune
  "harmonics as a detuning in semitones: unison at 0.5, then a fifth, an
octave, an octave and a fifth and two octaves either way, with flat spots on
each (Plaits' ComputeDetuning)"
  (lambda (harmonics:SAMPLE)
    (let ((d (macro_clamp (- (* 2.05 harmonics) 1.025) -1.0 1.0))
          (sign (if (< d 0.0) -1.0 1.0))
          (x (* d sign 3.9999))
          (i:i64 (convert x))
          (frac (- x (convert i SAMPLE)))
          (a (macro_va_interval i))
          (b (macro_va_interval (+ i 1))))
      ;; squashing the fraction twice makes the flat spots
      (set! frac (* frac frac (- 3.0 (* 2.0 frac))))
      (set! frac (* frac frac (- 3.0 (* 2.0 frac))))
      (* sign (+ a (* frac (- b a)))))))

(bind-func macro_va_c
  (lambda ()
    (let ((primary (macro_varishape_c 0.0))
          (auxiliary (macro_varishape_c 0.25))
          (square (macro_varishape_c 0.0))
          (saw (macro_varsaw_c))
          (r (macro_ramp_make 12))
          (sync_amount:SAMPLE 0.0) (detune:SAMPLE 0.0) (square_gain:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (saw_gain:SAMPLE 0.0) (norm:SAMPLE 1.0) (x:SAMPLE 0.0) (jump:i1 #f)
          (a:SAMPLE 0.0) (b:SAMPLE 0.0))
      ;; the ramps: 0 primary f, 1 detuned f, 2 primary sync f, 3 detuned sync f,
      ;; 4 pw, 5 shape, 6 square pw, 7 square sync f, 8 saw pw, 9 saw shape,
      ;; 10 square gain, 11 saw gain
      (lambda (ctl:i64 f0:SAMPLE harmonics:SAMPLE timbre:SAMPLE morph:SAMPLE out:SAMPLE*)
        (if (<> ctl MACRO_SAMPLE)
            (begin
              (set! jump (>= ctl MACRO_NOTE_START))
              (set! sync_amount (* timbre timbre))
              (set! detune (macro_va_detune harmonics))
              (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr r 0) f0 jump)
              (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr r 1) (* f0 (semitones detune)) jump)
              (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr r 2) (* f0 (semitones (* 48.0 sync_amount))) jump)
              (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr r 3) (* f0 (semitones (+ detune (* 48.0 sync_amount)))) jump)
              (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr r 4) (macro_clamp (+ 0.5 (* 1.46 (- morph 0.66))) 0.5 0.995) jump)
              (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr r 5) (macro_clamp (* 1.5 morph) 0.0 1.0) jump)
              ;; OUT's square: off at timbre 0.0, a narrow pulse widening to
              ;; square at 0.5, then synced ever higher
              (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr r 6) (macro_clamp (- (* 1.3 timbre) 0.15) 0.005 0.5) jump)
              (set! x (if (< timbre 0.5) 0.0 (* 192.0 (- timbre 0.5) (- timbre 0.5))))
              (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr r 7) (* f0 (semitones x)) jump)
              (set! square_gain (macro_clamp (* 8.0 timbre) 0.0 1.0))
              ;; OUT's saw: a skewed triangle at morph 0.0, a notched saw, a
              ;; plain saw at 0.5, then narrowing and fading
              (set! x (if (< morph 0.5) (+ morph 0.5) (- 1.0 (* 2.0 (- morph 0.5)))))
              (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr r 8) (macro_clamp (* 1.1 x) 0.005 1.0) jump)
              (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr r 9) (macro_clamp (- 10.0 (* 21.0 morph)) 0.0 1.0) jump)
              (set! saw_gain (macro_clamp (* 8.0 (- 1.0 morph)) 0.02 1.0))
              (set! norm (/ 1.0 (if (> square_gain saw_gain) square_gain saw_gain)))
              (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr r 10) (* 0.3 norm square_gain) jump)
              (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr r 11) (* 0.5 norm saw_gain) jump)))
        (let ((restart (= ctl MACRO_NOTE_RESET))
              (f (macro_ramp (pref-ptr r 0)))
              (fd (macro_ramp (pref-ptr r 1)))
              (fs (macro_ramp (pref-ptr r 2)))
              (fds (macro_ramp (pref-ptr r 3)))
              (pw (macro_ramp (pref-ptr r 4)))
              (shape (macro_ramp (pref-ptr r 5)))
              (square_pw (macro_ramp (pref-ptr r 6)))
              (square_f (macro_ramp (pref-ptr r 7)))
              (saw_pw (macro_ramp (pref-ptr r 8)))
              (saw_shape (macro_ramp (pref-ptr r 9)))
              (gs (macro_ramp (pref-ptr r 10)))
              (gw (macro_ramp (pref-ptr r 11))))
          ;; AUX: the difference of the two synced oscillators
          (set! a (primary f fs pw shape restart))
          (set! b (auxiliary fd fds pw shape restart))
          (pset! out 1 (* 0.5 (- b a)))
          ;; OUT: the square plus the detuned saw
          (pset! out 0 (+ (* gs (square f square_f square_pw 1.0 restart))
                          (* gw (saw fd saw_pw saw_shape restart))))
          void)))))

;; engine 1: waveshaping (Plaits' WaveshapingEngine)

(bind-func static macro_tame
  "how much of a shaper's effect to keep, so that a waveform with harmonics up
to f0 * harmonics, made `order` times richer, stays below the Nyquist frequency"
  (lambda (f0:SAMPLE harmonics:SAMPLE order:SAMPLE)
    (let ((f (* f0 harmonics))
          (max_f (/ 0.5 order))
          (a (macro_clamp (- 1.0 (/ (- f max_f) (- 0.5 max_f))) 0.0 1.0)))
      (* a a a))))

(bind-func macro_fold_c
  (lambda ()
    (let ((slope (macro_slope_c))
          (triangle (macro_slope_c))
          (r (macro_ramp_make 4))
          (os_o (os_make)) (os_a (os_make)) (k:i64 0) (steps:i64 1)
          (o0:SAMPLE 0.0) (o1:SAMPLE 0.0) (fo:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (f0r:SAMPLE 0.0) (steep:SAMPLE 0.0) (amount:SAMPLE 0.0) (att:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (x:SAMPLE 0.0) (jump:i1 #f))
      ;; the ramps: 0 slope pw, 1 waveshaper, 2 folder gain, 3 overtone gain
      (lambda (ctl:i64 f0:SAMPLE harmonics:SAMPLE timbre:SAMPLE morph:SAMPLE out:SAMPLE*)
        (if (<> ctl MACRO_SAMPLE)
            (begin
              (set! jump (>= ctl MACRO_NOTE_START))
              (set! f0r f0)
              (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr r 0) (+ 0.5 (* 0.45 morph)) jump)
              ;; estimate how rich the shaped wave will be, and hold the
              ;; shaper and folder back on high notes so they don't alias
              (set! steep (+ 3.0 (* 5.0 (fabs (- morph 0.5)))))
              (set! amount (* 2.0 (fabs (- harmonics 0.5))))
              (set! att (macro_tame f0 steep 16.0))
              (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr r 1) (+ 0.5 (* att (- harmonics 0.5))) jump)
              (set! att (macro_tame f0 (* steep (+ 3.0 (* 5.0 amount att))) 12.0))
              (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr r 2) (+ 0.03 (* 0.46 timbre att)) jump)
              (set! x (* timbre (- 2.0 timbre)))
              (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr r 3) (* x (- 2.0 x)) jump)))
        (let ((restart (= ctl MACRO_NOTE_RESET))
              (pwr (macro_ramp (pref-ptr r 0)))
              (shape (* 3.9999 (macro_ramp (pref-ptr r 1))))
              (wf_gain (macro_ramp (pref-ptr r 2)))
              (overtone (macro_ramp (pref-ptr r 3)))
              (si:i64 (convert shape))
              (sf (- shape (convert si SAMPLE)))
              (c1 (pref-ptr macro_ws_table (* si 257)))
              (c2 (pref-ptr macro_ws_table (* (+ si 1) 257))))
          (if restart (begin (os_clear os_o) (os_clear os_a)))
          (set! steps (if (> f0r MACRO_OS_F) 2 1))
          (set! fo (if (> f0r MACRO_OS_F) (* 0.5 f0r) f0r))
          (dotimes (k steps)
            (let ((s (slope fo pwr (and restart (= k 0))))
                  (tri (triangle fo 0.5 (and restart (= k 0))))
                  ;; waveshape the slope through two neighbouring curves and blend
                  (pos (macro_clamp (+ 128.0 (* 127.0 s)) 0.0 255.99))
                  (wi:i64 (convert pos))
                  (pf (- pos (convert wi SAMPLE)))
                  (y1 (+ (pref c1 wi) (* pf (- (pref c1 (+ wi 1)) (pref c1 wi)))))
                  (y2 (+ (pref c2 wi) (* pf (- (pref c2 (+ wi 1)) (pref c2 wi)))))
                  (index (+ 0.5 (* wf_gain (+ y1 (* sf (- y2 y1))))))
                  (sine (macro_sine (+ 0.5 (* 0.25 tri))))
                  (fold2 (* -1.0 (macro_hermite (pref-ptr macro_fold_table 517) index 512.0))))
              (set! o0 (macro_hermite (pref-ptr macro_fold_table 1) index 512.0))
              ;; inverted, so that it adds to OUT rather than cancelling it when
              ;; the two are mixed (on Plaits they're separate sockets)
              (set! o1 (* -1.0 (+ sine (* overtone (- fold2 sine)))))
              (pset! os_o k o0)
              (pset! os_a k o1)))
          (if (= steps 2)
              (begin (pset! out 0 (os_down2 os_o)) (pset! out 1 (os_down2 os_a)))
              (begin (pset! out 0 o0) (pset! out 1 o1)))
          void)))))

;; engine 2: two-operator FM (Plaits' FMEngine)

(bind-val MACRO_FM_REACH SAMPLE 0.33)

(bind-func macro_fm_c
  (lambda ()
    (let ((carrier_phase:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (modulator_phase:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (sub_phase:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (previous:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (carrier_head:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (sub_head:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (fir:SAMPLE* (zalloc 4))
          (r (macro_ramp_make 4))
          (ratio:SAMPLE 0.0) (x:SAMPLE 0.0) (note:SAMPLE 0.0) (taming:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (rat:SAMPLE 1.0) (idx:SAMPLE 0.0) (cap:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (jump:i1 #f) (j:i64 0))
      ;; half of an 8-tap lowpass, used to come back down from 4x
      (pfill! fir 0.02442415 0.09297315 0.16712938 0.21547332)
      ;; the ramps: 0 carrier f, 1 modulator f, 2 modulation index, 3 feedback
      (lambda (ctl:i64 f0:SAMPLE harmonics:SAMPLE timbre:SAMPLE morph:SAMPLE out:SAMPLE*)
        (if (<> ctl MACRO_SAMPLE)
            (begin
              (set! jump (>= ctl MACRO_NOTE_START))
              ;; frequencies are per oversampled step, so a quarter of f0
              (set! x (* 128.0 harmonics))
              (set! j (convert x))
              (set! x (- x (convert j SAMPLE)))
              (set! ratio (+ (pref macro_fm_table j) (* x (- (pref macro_fm_table (+ j 1)) (pref macro_fm_table j)))))
              (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr r 0) (* 0.25 f0) jump)
              (set! rat (semitones ratio))
              (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr r 1) (macro_clamp (* 0.25 f0 rat) 0.0 0.5) jump)
              ;; less modulation for high modulators, to keep the sidebands
              ;; below the Nyquist frequency. `note` is the modulator's pitch
              ;; in Plaits' terms (MIDI note, two octaves down at 4x)
              (set! note (+ 45.0 ratio (* 17.31234 (log (/ (* f0 48000.0) 440.0)))))
              (set! taming (macro_clamp (- 1.0 (* 0.025 (- note 72.0))) 0.0 1.0))
              (set! idx (* 2.0 timbre timbre taming taming))
              ;; The sidebands reach about (2 pi index + 2) modulator
              ;; frequencies above the carrier. Keep that below MACRO_FM_REACH
              ;; of the sample rate, bending the index over smoothly as it
              ;; nears the limit
              (set! cap (/ (- (/ MACRO_FM_REACH (* rat f0)) 2.0) STWOPI))
              (if (< cap 0.01) (set! cap 0.01))
              (set! idx (/ (* idx cap) (sqrt (sqrt (+ (* idx idx idx idx) (* cap cap cap cap))))))
              (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr r 2) idx jump)
              (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr r 3) (- (* 2.0 morph) 1.0) jump)))
        (if (= ctl MACRO_NOTE_RESET)
            (begin
              (set! modulator_phase 0.0) (set! carrier_phase 0.0) (set! sub_phase 0.0)
              (set! previous 0.0) (set! carrier_head 0.0) (set! sub_head 0.0)))
        (let ((fc (macro_ramp (pref-ptr r 0)))
              (fm (macro_ramp (pref-ptr r 1)))
              (index (macro_ramp (pref-ptr r 2)))
              (feedback (macro_ramp (pref-ptr r 3)))
              (phase_fb (if (< feedback 0.0) (* 0.5 feedback feedback) 0.0))
              (modulator_fb (if (> feedback 0.0) (* 0.25 feedback feedback) 0.0))
              ;; local copies of the state, which the compiler can keep in
              ;; registers through the loop
              (mp modulator_phase) (cp carrier_phase) (sp sub_phase) (prev previous)
              (carrier_acc carrier_head) (sub_acc sub_head)
              (modulator:SAMPLE 0.0) (carrier:SAMPLE 0.0) (sub:SAMPLE 0.0)
              (carrier_tail:SAMPLE 0.0) (sub_tail:SAMPLE 0.0)
              (k:i64 0))
          (dotimes (k 4)
            (set! mp (+ mp (* fm (+ 1.0 (* prev phase_fb)))))
            (if (>= mp 1.0) (set! mp (- mp 1.0)))
            (set! cp (+ cp fc))
            (if (>= cp 1.0) (set! cp (- cp 1.0)))
            (set! sp (+ sp (* 0.5 fc)))
            (if (>= sp 1.0) (set! sp (- sp 1.0)))
            (set! modulator (macro_sine (+ mp (* modulator_fb prev))))
            (set! carrier (macro_sine (+ cp (* index modulator))))
            (set! sub (macro_sine (+ sp (* 0.25 index carrier))))
            (set! prev (+ prev (* 0.05 (- carrier prev))))
            ;; the 8-tap FIR, run as two overlapping halves
            (set! carrier_acc (+ carrier_acc (* carrier (pref fir (- 3 k)))))
            (set! carrier_tail (+ carrier_tail (* carrier (pref fir k))))
            (set! sub_acc (+ sub_acc (* sub (pref fir (- 3 k)))))
            (set! sub_tail (+ sub_tail (* sub (pref fir k)))))
          (pset! out 0 carrier_acc)
          (pset! out 1 sub_acc)
          (set! modulator_phase mp) (set! carrier_phase cp) (set! sub_phase sp) (set! previous prev)
          (set! carrier_head carrier_tail)
          (set! sub_head sub_tail)
          void)))))

;; engine 3: granular formant oscillators (Plaits' GrainEngine)

(bind-func static macro_grain_carrier
  "the window a grainlet's burst is shaped by: morph 0.0 is narrow, 0.33
is a raised cosine, then it widens and skews"
  (lambda (phase_in:SAMPLE shape_in:SAMPLE)
    (let ((shape (* 3.0 shape_in))
          (i:i64 (convert shape))
          (t (- 1.0 (- shape (convert i SAMPLE))))
          (phase phase_in)
          (bp:SAMPLE 0.0))
      (cond ((= i 0)
             (set! phase (* phase (+ 1.0 (* 15.0 t t t))))
             (if (>= phase 1.0) (set! phase 1.0))
             (set! phase (+ phase 0.75)))
            ((= i 1)
             (set! bp (+ 0.001 (* 0.499 t t t)))
             (set! phase (if (< phase bp)
                             (* phase (/ 0.5 bp))
                             (+ 0.5 (/ (* 0.5 (- phase bp)) (- 1.0 bp)))))
             (set! phase (+ phase 0.75)))
            (else
              (set! t (- 1.0 t))
              (set! phase (+ 0.25 (* phase (+ 0.5 (* 14.5 t t t)))))
              (if (>= phase 0.75) (set! phase 0.75))))
      (* 0.25 (+ 1.0 (macro_sine phase))))))

(bind-func static macro_grainlet
  (lambda (carrier_phase:SAMPLE formant_phase:SAMPLE shape:SAMPLE bleed:SAMPLE)
    (/ (* (macro_grain_carrier carrier_phase shape) (+ (macro_sine formant_phase) bleed))
       (+ 1.0 bleed))))

(bind-func macro_grainlet_c
  "Plaits' GrainletOscillator: a sine at the formant frequency, restarted
and windowed on every cycle of the carrier"
  (lambda ()
    (let ((carrier_phase:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (formant_phase:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (next:SAMPLE 0.0))
      (lambda (fc:SAMPLE ff:SAMPLE shape:SAMPLE bleed:SAMPLE)
        (let ((f0 (if (> fc 0.125) 0.125 fc))
              (f1 (if (> ff 0.25) 0.25 ff))
              (cur next)
              (reset_time:SAMPLE 0.0)
              (jump:SAMPLE 0.0))
          (set! next 0.0)
          (set! carrier_phase (+ carrier_phase f0))
          (if (>= carrier_phase 1.0)
              (begin
                ;; the restart is a step: round it off
                (set! carrier_phase (- carrier_phase 1.0))
                (set! reset_time (/ carrier_phase f0))
                (set! jump (- (macro_grainlet 0.0 0.0 shape bleed)
                              (macro_grainlet 1.0 (+ formant_phase (* (- 1.0 reset_time) f1)) shape bleed)))
                (set! cur (+ cur (* jump (macro_blep_this reset_time))))
                (set! next (+ next (* jump (macro_blep_next reset_time))))
                (set! formant_phase (* reset_time f1))
                void)
              (begin
                (set! formant_phase (+ formant_phase f1))
                (if (>= formant_phase 1.0) (set! formant_phase (- formant_phase 1.0)))
                void))
          (set! next (+ next (macro_grainlet carrier_phase formant_phase shape bleed)))
          cur)))))

(bind-func static macro_z
  (lambda (c:SAMPLE d:SAMPLE f:SAMPLE shape_in:SAMPLE mode:SAMPLE)
    (let ((ramp_down (* 0.5 (+ 1.0 (macro_sine (+ 0.25 (* 0.5 d))))))
          (offset:SAMPLE 1.0)
          (phase_shift:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (shape shape_in)
          (contour:SAMPLE 0.0))
      (if (< mode 0.333)
          (begin (set! offset 1.0) (set! phase_shift (+ 0.25 (* 1.5 mode))) void)
          (begin
            (set! phase_shift (- 0.7495 (* 0.75 (- mode 0.33))))
            (set! offset (if (< mode 0.666) (* -1.0 (macro_sine phase_shift)) 0.001))
            void))
      (if (< shape 0.5)
          (begin
            (set! shape (* 2.0 shape))
            (if (>= c 0.5) (set! ramp_down (* ramp_down shape)))
            (set! contour (+ 1.0 (* shape (- (macro_sine (+ c 0.25)) 1.0))))
            void)
          (begin (set! contour (macro_sine (+ c (* 0.5 shape)))) void))
      (* contour (- (* ramp_down (+ offset (macro_sine (+ f phase_shift)))) offset)))))

(bind-func macro_z_c
  "Plaits' ZOscillator: a sine at the formant frequency, restarted twice per
carrier cycle and shaped by a window, in the manner of Casio's CZ resonant
waveforms"
  (lambda ()
    (let ((carrier_phase:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (discontinuity_phase:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (formant_phase:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (next:SAMPLE 0.0))
      (lambda (fc:SAMPLE ff:SAMPLE shape:SAMPLE mode:SAMPLE)
        (let ((f0 (if (> fc 0.125) 0.125 fc))
              (f1 (if (> ff 0.25) 0.25 ff))
              (cur next)
              (reset_time:SAMPLE 0.0)
              (wrapped:i1 #f)
              (jump:SAMPLE 0.0))
          (set! next 0.0)
          (set! discontinuity_phase (+ discontinuity_phase (* 2.0 f0)))
          (set! carrier_phase (+ carrier_phase f0))
          (if (>= discontinuity_phase 1.0)
              (begin
                (set! discontinuity_phase (- discontinuity_phase 1.0))
                (set! reset_time (/ discontinuity_phase (* 2.0 f0)))
                (set! wrapped (>= carrier_phase 1.0))
                (set! jump (- (macro_z (if wrapped 0.0 0.5) 0.0 0.0 shape mode)
                              (macro_z (if wrapped 1.0 0.5) 1.0
                                       (+ formant_phase (* (- 1.0 reset_time) f1)) shape mode)))
                (set! cur (+ cur (* jump (macro_blep_this reset_time))))
                (set! next (+ next (* jump (macro_blep_next reset_time))))
                (set! formant_phase (* reset_time f1))
                (if (> carrier_phase 1.0)
                    (set! carrier_phase (* 0.5 discontinuity_phase)))
                void)
              (begin
                (set! formant_phase (+ formant_phase f1))
                (if (>= formant_phase 1.0) (set! formant_phase (- formant_phase 1.0)))
                void))
          (if (>= carrier_phase 1.0) (set! carrier_phase (- carrier_phase 1.0)))
          (set! next (+ next (macro_z carrier_phase discontinuity_phase formant_phase shape mode)))
          cur)))))

(bind-func macro_grain_c
  (lambda ()
    (let ((grainlet1 (macro_grainlet_c))
          (grainlet2 (macro_grainlet_c))
          (zosc (macro_z_c))
          (dc1 (macro_dc_blocker_c))
          (dc2 (macro_dc_blocker_c))
          (r (macro_ramp_make 7))
          (bleed:SAMPLE 0.0) (f0r:SAMPLE 0.0) (jump:i1 #f))
      ;; the ramps: 0 formant f, 1 second formant f, 2 window shape, 3 bleed,
      ;; 4 Z resonance f, 5 Z window, 6 Z mode
      (lambda (ctl:i64 f0:SAMPLE harmonics:SAMPLE timbre:SAMPLE morph:SAMPLE out:SAMPLE*)
        (if (<> ctl MACRO_SAMPLE)
            (begin
              (set! jump (>= ctl MACRO_NOTE_START))
              (set! f0r f0)
              ;; the formant is a fixed frequency, MIDI note 24 to 108
              (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr r 0) (/ (midi2frq (+ 24.0 (* 84.0 timbre))) SRf) jump)
              (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr r 1) (* (/ (midi2frq (+ 24.0 (* 84.0 timbre))) SRf)
                                               (semitones (- (* 48.0 harmonics) 24.0)))
                             jump)
              ;; narrow windows alias on high notes, so ease them back to 0.33
              (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr r 2) (+ 0.33 (* (- morph 0.33) (macro_clamp (- 1.0 (* 24.0 f0)) 0.0 1.0)))
                             jump)
              (set! bleed (if (< harmonics 0.5) (- 1.0 (* 2.0 harmonics)) 0.0))
              (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr r 3) (* bleed (- 2.0 bleed)) jump)
              (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr r 4) (* f0 (semitones (* 96.0 timbre))) jump)
              (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr r 5) morph jump)
              (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr r 6) harmonics jump)))
        (let ((ff1 (macro_ramp (pref-ptr r 0)))
              (ff2 (macro_ramp (pref-ptr r 1)))
              (shape (macro_ramp (pref-ptr r 2)))
              (bl (macro_ramp (pref-ptr r 3)))
              (zf (macro_ramp (pref-ptr r 4)))
              (zshape (macro_ramp (pref-ptr r 5)))
              (zmode (macro_ramp (pref-ptr r 6))))
          (pset! out 0 (dc1 (+ (grainlet1 f0r ff1 shape bl) (grainlet2 f0r ff2 shape bl)) (* 0.3 f0r)))
          (pset! out 1 (dc2 (zosc f0r zf zshape zmode) (* 0.3 f0r)))
          void)))))

;; engine 4: additive (Plaits' AdditiveEngine)

(bind-func macro_harmonic_c
  (lambda ()
    (let ((spectrum:SAMPLE* (zalloc 36)) ;; 0-23 OUT's harmonics 1-24, 24-35 AUX's 1-12
          (organ:i64* (zalloc 8))
          (r (macro_ramp_make 36))
          (phase:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (f0r:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (k:i64 0) (i:i64 0) (j:i64 0) (n:i64 0)
          (centroid:SAMPLE 0.0) (slope:SAMPLE 0.0) (bumps:SAMPLE 0.0) (raw:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (margin:SAMPLE 0.0) (centre:SAMPLE 0.0) (order:SAMPLE 0.0) (gain:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (sum:SAMPLE 0.0) (fk:SAMPLE 0.0) (smooth:SAMPLE 0.0) (jump:i1 #f))
      ;; the drawbar harmonics, counting from 0
      (pfill! organ 0 1 2 3 5 7 9 11)
      (dotimes (i 36) (pset! spectrum i 0.0))
      ;; Plaits' UpdateAmplitudes: a peak at the centroid, triangular with a
      ;; slope, rippled by bumps, smoothed over time and normalised to sum to 1
      (let ((update (lambda (offset:i64 count:i64 drawbars:i1)
                      (set! margin (/ (- (/ 1.0 slope) 1.0) (+ 1.0 bumps)))
                      (set! centre (- (* centroid (+ (convert (- count 1) SAMPLE) margin)) (* 0.5 margin)))
                      (set! sum 0.001)
                      (dotimes (k count)
                        (set! order (* slope (fabs (- (convert k SAMPLE) centre))))
                        (set! gain (- 1.0 order))
                        (set! gain (+ gain (fabs gain)))
                        (set! gain (* gain gain (+ 1.0 (macro_sine (+ 0.25 (* order bumps))))))
                        (set! gain (* gain gain))
                        (set! gain (* gain gain))
                        (set! j (+ offset (if drawbars (pref organ k) k)))
                        (pset! spectrum j (+ (pref spectrum j) (* smooth (- gain (pref spectrum j)))))
                        (set! sum (+ sum (pref spectrum j))))
                      (dotimes (k count)
                        (set! j (+ offset (if drawbars (pref organ k) k)))
                        (pset! spectrum j (/ (pref spectrum j) sum)))
                      void)))
        (lambda (ctl:i64 f0:SAMPLE harmonics:SAMPLE timbre:SAMPLE morph:SAMPLE out:SAMPLE*)
          (if (<> ctl MACRO_SAMPLE)
              (begin
                (set! jump (>= ctl MACRO_NOTE_START))
                (set! f0r f0)
                (set! centroid timbre)
                (set! raw (* morph (- 1.0 (* 0.6 harmonics))))
                (set! slope (+ 0.01 (* 1.99 raw raw raw)))
                (set! bumps (* 16.0 harmonics harmonics))
                ;; Plaits' 0.001 per 4 kHz block: a time constant of 0.25 s
                (set! smooth (* 4.0 (/ (convert MACRO_BLOCK SAMPLE) SRf)))
                (update 0 24 #f)
                (update 24 8 #t)
                ;; each harmonic fades out as it nears the Nyquist frequency
                (dotimes (i 36)
                  (set! fk (* f0 (convert (+ 1 (if (< i 24) i (- i 24))) SAMPLE)))
                  (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr r i)
                                 (* (pref spectrum i) (if (< fk 0.5) (- 1.0 (* 2.0 fk)) 0.0))
                                 jump))))
          (set! phase (+ phase (if (> f0r 0.5) 0.5 f0r)))
          (if (>= phase 1.0) (set! phase (- phase 1.0)))
          ;; Chebyshev recursion: from x = sin(phase), T(k+1) = 2x T(k) - T(k-1)
          ;; gives every harmonic with a multiply and an add
          (let ((two_x (* 2.0 (macro_sine phase)))
                (previous:SAMPLE 1.0)
                (current (* 0.5 two_x))
                (temp:SAMPLE 0.0)
                (sum_out:SAMPLE 0.0)
                (sum_aux:SAMPLE 0.0)
                (h:i64 0))
            (dotimes (h 24)
              (set! sum_out (+ sum_out (* current (macro_ramp (pref-ptr r h)))))
              (if (< h 12)
                  (set! sum_aux (+ sum_aux (* current (macro_ramp (pref-ptr r (+ 24 h)))))))
              (set! temp current)
              (set! current (- (* two_x current) previous))
              (set! previous temp))
            (pset! out 0 sum_out)
            (pset! out 1 sum_aux)
            void))))))

;; engine 5: swarm (Plaits' SwarmEngine)

(bind-val MACRO_SWARM i64 8)

(bind-func macro_swarm_c
  (lambda ()
    (let ((n MACRO_SWARM)
          ;; each grain's envelope (Plaits' GrainEnvelope)
          (from:SAMPLE* (zalloc n))
          (interval:SAMPLE* (zalloc n))
          (gphase:SAMPLE* (zalloc n))
          (gfm:SAMPLE* (zalloc n))
          (amp:SAMPLE* (zalloc n))
          (previous_size:SAMPLE* (zalloc n))
          (filter_coeff:SAMPLE* (zalloc n))
          ;; each saw and sine
          (saw_phase:SAMPLE* (zalloc n))
          (saw_next:SAMPLE* (zalloc n))
          (sine_x:SAMPLE* (zalloc n))
          (sine_y:SAMPLE* (zalloc n))
          (saw_f (macro_ramp_make n))
          (saw_gain (macro_ramp_make n))
          (sine_eps (macro_ramp_make n))
          (sine_gain (macro_ramp_make n))
          (i:i64 0)
          (density:SAMPLE 0.0) (spread:SAMPLE 0.0) (size_ratio:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (rank:SAMPLE 0.0) (rnd:SAMPLE 0.0) (randomise:i1 #f) (target:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (x:SAMPLE 0.0) (f:SAMPLE 0.0) (a:SAMPLE 0.0) (norm:SAMPLE 0.0) (jump:i1 #f)
          (peak_out:SAMPLE 0.5) (peak_aux:SAMPLE 0.5))
      (dotimes (i n)
        (pset! from i 0.0) (pset! interval i 1.0) (pset! gphase i 1.0) (pset! gfm i 0.0)
        (pset! amp i 0.5) (pset! previous_size i 0.0) (pset! filter_coeff i 0.0)
        ;; start the saws and sines at random phases, so that a note doesn't
        ;; begin with all eight in step
        (set! rnd (random))
        (pset! saw_phase i rnd) (pset! saw_next i rnd)
        (set! rnd (random))
        (pset! sine_x i (cos (* STWOPI rnd))) (pset! sine_y i (sin (* STWOPI rnd))))
      (lambda (ctl:i64 f0:SAMPLE harmonics:SAMPLE timbre:SAMPLE morph:SAMPLE out:SAMPLE*)
        (if (<> ctl MACRO_SAMPLE)
            (begin
              (set! jump (>= ctl MACRO_NOTE_START))
              ;; grains per block: timbre 0.0 is one every few seconds, 1.0 is ~200 a second
              (set! density (* 0.025 (midi2frq (* 120.0 timbre)) (/ (convert MACRO_BLOCK SAMPLE) SRf)))
              (set! spread (* harmonics harmonics harmonics))
              (set! size_ratio (* 0.25 (semitones (* 84.0 (- 1.0 morph)))))
              (dotimes (i n)
                ;; Plaits ranks its voices (i - 3) / 3 (an integer division of
                ;; 7 by 2), from -1.0 to 1.33
                (set! rank (/ (- (convert i SAMPLE) 3.0) 3.0))
                ;; step the grain envelope; a new note starts a burst of
                ;; fast grains which slow down, one after another
                (set! randomise #f)
                (if jump
                    (begin (pset! gphase i 0.5) (pset! gfm i 16.0) (set! randomise #t) void)
                    (begin
                      (pset! gphase i (+ (pref gphase i) (* density (pref gfm i))))
                      (if (>= (pref gphase i) 1.0)
                          (begin
                            (pset! gphase i (- (pref gphase i) (floor (pref gphase i))))
                            (set! randomise #t)))
                      void))
                (if randomise
                    (begin
                      (pset! from i (+ (pref from i) (pref interval i)))
                      (set! rnd (random))
                      (pset! interval i (- rnd (pref from i)))
                      (set! rnd (random))
                      (pset! gfm i (* (pref gfm i) (+ 0.8 (* 0.2 rnd))))))
                ;; long grains (size_ratio >= 1) fade in and out; short ones
                ;; become a continuous glide from one random pitch to the next
                (set! target 1.0)
                (if (>= size_ratio 1.0)
                    (begin
                      (set! x (macro_clamp (* size_ratio (- (pref gphase i) 0.5)) -1.0 1.0))
                      (set! target (* 0.5 (+ 1.0 (macro_sine (+ 1.25 (* 0.5 x))))))))
                (if (<> (>= size_ratio 1.0) (>= (pref previous_size i) 1.0))
                    (pset! filter_coeff i 0.5))
                (pset! filter_coeff i (* 0.95 (pref filter_coeff i)))
                (pset! previous_size i size_ratio)
                (pset! amp i (+ (pref amp i) (* (- 0.5 (pref filter_coeff i)) (- target (pref amp i)))))
                (set! a (/ (pref amp i) (convert n SAMPLE)))
                (set! x (if (< size_ratio 1.0)
                            (- (* 2.0 (+ (pref from i) (* (pref interval i) (pref gphase i)))) 1.0)
                            (pref from i)))
                (set! f (* f0 (semitones (* 48.0 x spread rank))
                           (+ 1.0 (* 0.25 rank (+ rank 0.01) spread))))
                (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr saw_f i) (if (> f 0.25) 0.25 f) jump)
                (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr saw_gain i) a jump)
                (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr sine_eps i) (* 2.0 (sin (* SPI (if (> f 0.25) 0.25 f)))) jump)
                (macro_ramp_to (pref-ptr sine_gain i) (if (< f 0.25) (* a (- 1.0 (* 4.0 f))) 0.0) jump)
                ;; keep the sine's rotation from drifting in amplitude
                (set! norm (+ (* (pref sine_x i) (pref sine_x i)) (* (pref sine_y i) (pref sine_y i))))
                (if (or (< norm 0.5) (> norm 2.0))
                    (begin
                      (set! norm (/ 1.0 (sqrt norm)))
                      (pset! sine_x i (* norm (pref sine_x i)))
                      (pset! sine_y i (* norm (pref sine_y i)))))
                (set! size_ratio (* 0.97 size_ratio)))))
        (let ((saws:SAMPLE 0.0)
              (sines:SAMPLE 0.0)
              (o:i64 0))
          (dotimes (o n)
            ;; a saw with a polyBLEP at the wrap (AdditiveSawOscillator)
            (let ((sf (macro_ramp (pref-ptr saw_f o)))
                  (cur (pref saw_next o))
                  (next:SAMPLE 0.0)
                  (p (+ (pref saw_phase o) sf))
                  (t:SAMPLE 0.0)
                  (e (macro_ramp (pref-ptr sine_eps o)))
                  (sx (pref sine_x o))
                  (sy (pref sine_y o)))
              (if (>= p 1.0)
                  (begin
                    (set! p (- p 1.0))
                    (set! t (/ p sf))
                    (set! cur (- cur (macro_blep_this t)))
                    (set! next (- next (macro_blep_next t)))))
              (pset! saw_phase o p)
              (pset! saw_next o (+ next p))
              (set! saws (+ saws (* (macro_ramp (pref-ptr saw_gain o)) (- (* 2.0 cur) 1.0))))
              ;; a sine made by rotating a point around a circle
              (set! sx (+ sx (* e sy)))
              (set! sy (- sy (* e sx)))
              (pset! sine_x o sx)
              (pset! sine_y o sy)
              (set! sines (+ sines (* (macro_ramp (pref-ptr sine_gain o)) sx)))))
          (pset! out 0 saws)
          (pset! out 1 sines))
        ;; sixteen free-running oscillators sum to an unpredictable level, so
        ;; Plaits boosts them and rides a limiter: the gain drops at once on
        ;; a peak and recovers over about a second
        (set! x (* 3.0 (pref out 0)))
        (set! a (fabs x))
        (set! peak_out (+ peak_out (* (if (> a peak_out) 0.05 0.00002) (- a peak_out))))
        (pset! out 0 (* 0.8 x (if (> peak_out 1.0) (/ 1.0 peak_out) 1.0)))
        (set! x (* 3.0 (pref out 1)))
        (set! a (fabs x))
        (set! peak_aux (+ peak_aux (* (if (> a peak_aux) 0.05 0.00002) (- a peak_aux))))
        (pset! out 1 (* 0.8 x (if (> peak_aux 1.0) (/ 1.0 peak_aux) 1.0)))
        void))))

;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
;; the voice ;;
;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;

(bind-val MACRO_ENGINES i64 6)

(bind-func static macro_engine_gain
  "OUT and AUX gains for each engine (AUX in the odd entries), which bring a
full-velocity note to about -12 dBFS"
  (lambda (engine:i64 aux:i1)
    (let ((g:SAMPLE 1.0))
      (cond ((= engine 0) (set! g (if aux 0.3 0.39)))
            ((= engine 1) (set! g (if aux 0.36 0.36)))
            ((= engine 2) (set! g (if aux 0.25 0.25)))
            ((= engine 3) (set! g (if aux 0.33 0.36)))
            ((= engine 4) (set! g (if aux 0.27 0.33)))
            (else (set! g (if aux 0.36 0.36))))
      g)))

(bind-func macro_voice_c
  (lambda (p:SAMPLE*)
    (let ((engines:MacroEngine* (zalloc MACRO_ENGINES))
          (engine:MacroEngine null)
          (index:i64 -1)
          (previous_index:i64 -1)
          (osc:SAMPLE* (zalloc 2))
          (ctl:i64 0)
          (countdown:i64 0)
          (f0:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (dt (/ (convert MACRO_BLOCK SAMPLE) SRf))
          ;; the decay envelope, and the vactrol in the low-pass gate
          (decay_env:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (vactrol:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (pinging:i1 #f)
          (peak:SAMPLE 1.0)
          (gain (macro_ramp_make 1))
          (hf_bleed:SAMPLE 0.0)
          ;; the gate's filter (stmlib's Svf), one each for OUT and AUX
          (g:SAMPLE 0.0) (h:SAMPLE 0.0) (r:SAMPLE 2.5)
          ;; the DC blockers. Each starts as a running mean over the note so far
          ;; (with a quarter of a period's worth of samples counted as already
          ;; seen), so that the offset of a pulse wave is gone within a few
          ;; periods, and settles to a one-pole highpass at 5 Hz
          (dc_a:SAMPLE 0.0) (dc_b:SAMPLE 0.0) (dc_coeff (* STWOPI (/ 5.0 SRf)))
          (dc_c:SAMPLE 0.0) (dc_n0:SAMPLE 1.0) (dc_k:SAMPLE 0.0)
          ;; a note starting on a voice which is still sounding fades the old
          ;; one out over 5 ms first; the new one begins when that is done
          (fade:i64 0) (fade_len:i64 (convert (/ SRf 200.0) i64)) (pending:i1 #f)
          (begin_now:i1 #f) (next_vel:SAMPLE 0.0) (fg:SAMPLE 1.0)
          ;; harmonics, timbre and morph glide towards their settings with a
          ;; time constant of 10 ms, taken once a block
          (hs:SAMPLE 0.0) (ts:SAMPLE 0.0) (ms:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (sm:SAMPLE (- 1.0 (exp (/ -2400.0 SRf))))
          (s1:SAMPLE 0.0) (s2:SAMPLE 0.0) (s3:SAMPLE 0.0) (s4:SAMPLE 0.0)
          ;; the attack and release envelope
          (amp_env:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (attack:SAMPLE -1.0) (release:SAMPLE -1.0)
          (attack_coeff:SAMPLE 0.0) (release_coeff:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (out_gain:SAMPLE 0.0) (aux_gain:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (aux_l:SAMPLE 0.0) (aux_r:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (decay:SAMPLE -1.0) (colour:SAMPLE -1.0) (short_decay:SAMPLE 0.0) (tail_decay:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (level:SAMPLE 0.0) (err:SAMPLE 0.0) (v4:SAMPLE 0.0) (tail:SAMPLE 0.0)
          (amount:SAMPLE 0.0) (harmonics:SAMPLE 0.0) (timbre:SAMPLE 0.0) (morph:SAMPLE 0.0) (x:SAMPLE 0.0))
      (pset! engines 0 (macro_va_c))
      (pset! engines 1 (macro_fold_c))
      (pset! engines 2 (macro_fm_c))
      (pset! engines 3 (macro_grain_c))
      (pset! engines 4 (macro_harmonic_c))
      (pset! engines 5 (macro_swarm_c))
      (lambda (v:Voice* out:SAMPLE*)
        (set! begin_now #f)
        (if (voice_start? v)
            (begin
              (set! next_vel (voice_vel v))
              (if (> (* amp_env vactrol) 0.0005)
                  (begin (set! fade fade_len) (set! pending #t) void)
                  (begin (set! begin_now #t) void))))
        (if (> fade 0)
            (begin
              (set! fade (- fade 1))
              (if (and (= fade 0) pending)
                  (begin (set! pending #f) (set! begin_now #t)))
              void))
        (if begin_now
            (begin
              ;; ping the vactrol open, as far as the velocity says: Plaits'
              ;; curve for its LEVEL input, which squashes towards 1.0
              (set! peak (macro_clamp (/ (* 1.3 next_vel) (+ 0.3 next_vel)) 0.0 1.0))
              (set! pinging #t)
              (set! decay_env 1.0)
              (set! vactrol 0.0)
              (set! amp_env 0.0)
              (set! s1 0.0) (set! s2 0.0) (set! s3 0.0) (set! s4 0.0)
              (set! dc_a 0.0) (set! dc_b 0.0) (set! dc_k 0.0)
              (set! dc_n0 (/ SRf (* 4.0 (voice_freq v))))
              (macro_ramp_to gain 0.0 #t)
              void))
        (set! ctl MACRO_SAMPLE)
        (if begin_now (set! countdown 0))
        (set! countdown (- countdown 1))
        (if (<= countdown 0)
            (begin
              (set! countdown MACRO_BLOCK)
              (set! index (convert (macro_clamp (+ 0.5 (macro_engine p)) 0.0 (- (convert MACRO_ENGINES SAMPLE) 1.0)) i64))
              (set! engine (pref engines index))
              ;; a new note, or a change of engine, sets the engine's ramps at once
              (set! ctl (if begin_now
                            MACRO_NOTE_RESET
                            (if (<> index previous_index) MACRO_NOTE_START MACRO_BLOCK_START)))
              (set! previous_index index)
              (set! f0 (/ (voice_freq v) SRf))
              (if (or (<> decay (macro_decay p)) (<> colour (macro_colour p)))
                  (begin
                    (set! decay (macro_decay p))
                    (set! colour (macro_colour p))
                    ;; Plaits' rates per 4 kHz block, as rates per second times dt
                    (set! short_decay (* 200.0 dt (pow 2.0 (* -8.0 decay))))
                    (set! tail_decay (- (* 20.0 dt (pow 2.0 (+ colour (* -6.0 decay)))) short_decay))))
              (set! decay_env (* decay_env (- 1.0 (* 2.0 short_decay))))
              ;; the vactrol rises in about half a cycle of the note...
              (if pinging
                  (begin
                    (set! vactrol (+ vactrol (* 2.0 (voice_freq v) dt)))
                    (if (>= vactrol peak) (begin (set! vactrol peak) (set! pinging #f)))))
              ;; ...and then falls towards the sustain level, quickly at first
              ;; and then slowly as it closes
              (set! level (if pinging vactrol (* (macro_sustain p) peak (voice_gate v))))
              (set! err (- level vactrol))
              (set! v4 (* vactrol vactrol vactrol vactrol))
              (set! vactrol (+ vactrol (* err (if (> err 0.0)
                                                  (macro_clamp (* 2400.0 dt) 0.0 1.0)
                                                  (+ short_decay (* (- 1.0 v4) tail_decay))))))
              (set! v4 (* vactrol vactrol vactrol vactrol))
              (macro_ramp_to gain vactrol #f)
              ;; the filter closes from 14 kHz to 150 Hz with it
              (set! x (* 48000.0 (+ 0.003 (* 0.3 v4) (* 0.04 colour))))
              ;; Plaits' cheap tan(pi f), close below 8 kHz and low above
              (set! x (/ (macro_clamp x 20.0 (* 0.45 SRf)) SRf))
              (set! g (* x (+ SPI (* 11.5844 x x))))
              (set! h (/ 1.0 (+ 1.0 (* r g) (* g g))))
              (set! tail (- 1.0 vactrol))
              (set! tail (* tail tail))
              (set! hf_bleed (* (+ tail (* (- 1.0 tail) colour)) colour colour))
              ;; the decay envelope moves timbre and morph
              (if begin_now
                  (begin (set! hs (macro_harmonics p)) (set! ts (macro_timbre p)) (set! ms (macro_morph p)) void)
                  (begin
                    (set! hs (+ hs (* sm (- (macro_harmonics p) hs))))
                    (set! ts (+ ts (* sm (- (macro_timbre p) ts))))
                    (set! ms (+ ms (* sm (- (macro_morph p) ms))))
                    void))
              (set! amount (macro_timbre_env p))
              (set! timbre (macro_clamp (+ ts (* amount (fabs amount) decay_env)) 0.0 1.0))
              (set! amount (macro_morph_env p))
              (set! morph (macro_clamp (+ ms (* amount (fabs amount) decay_env)) 0.0 1.0))
              (set! harmonics (macro_clamp hs 0.0 1.0))
              (set! dc_c (/ 1.0 (+ dc_n0 dc_k)))
              (if (< dc_c dc_coeff) (set! dc_c dc_coeff))
              (set! dc_k (+ dc_k (convert MACRO_BLOCK SAMPLE)))
              ;; how much of OUT and AUX goes to each side
              (set! aux_l (macro_clamp (- (macro_aux p) (* 0.5 (macro_width p))) 0.0 1.0))
              (set! aux_r (macro_clamp (+ (macro_aux p) (* 0.5 (macro_width p))) 0.0 1.0))
              (set! out_gain (* (macro_level p) (macro_engine_gain index #f)))
              (set! aux_gain (* (macro_level p) (macro_engine_gain index #t)))
              (if (<> attack (macro_attack p))
                  (begin (set! attack (macro_attack p)) (set! attack_coeff (smoothing_coeff attack))))
              (if (<> release (macro_release p))
                  (begin (set! release (macro_release p)) (set! release_coeff (smoothing_coeff release))))))
        (engine ctl f0 harmonics timbre morph osc)
        ;; block DC (a pulse wave has plenty), as the module's output coupling does
        (set! dc_a (+ dc_a (* dc_c (- (pref osc 0) dc_a))))
        (set! dc_b (+ dc_b (* dc_c (- (pref osc 1) dc_b))))
        ;; the low-pass gate: amplify by the vactrol, filter, and let the
        ;; highs bleed past by the colour
        (let ((vca (macro_ramp gain))
              (a (+ 1.0e-18 (* vca out_gain (- (pref osc 0) dc_a))))
              (b (+ 1.0e-18 (* vca aux_gain (- (pref osc 1) dc_b))))
              (hp (* h (- a (* r s1) (* g s1) s2)))
              (bp (+ (* g hp) s1))
              (lp_a (+ (* g bp) s2))
              (lp_b:SAMPLE 0.0))
          (set! s1 (+ (* g hp) bp))
          (set! s2 (+ (* g bp) lp_a))
          (set! hp (* h (- b (* r s3) (* g s3) s4)))
          (set! bp (+ (* g hp) s3))
          (set! lp_b (+ (* g bp) s4))
          (set! s3 (+ (* g hp) bp))
          (set! s4 (+ (* g bp) lp_b))
          (set! a (+ lp_a (* hf_bleed (- a lp_a))))
          (set! b (+ lp_b (* hf_bleed (- b lp_b))))
          ;; the attack and release envelope
          (set! amp_env (+ amp_env (* (if (> (voice_gate v) 0.5) attack_coeff release_coeff)
                                      (- (voice_gate v) amp_env))))
          (set! fg (if (> fade 0) (/ (convert fade SAMPLE) (convert fade_len SAMPLE)) 1.0))
          (frame_add_stereo out
                            (* amp_env fg (+ a (* aux_l (- b a))))
                            (* amp_env fg (+ a (* aux_r (- b a))))))
        (if (and (< (voice_gate v) 0.5) (not pinging) (not pending) (< (* amp_env vactrol) 0.0001))
            (voice_done v))
        void))))

(bind-func macro_make
  (lambda ()
    (let ((inst (inst_make "macro" 6 (macro_nparams)))
          (i:i64 0))
      (macro_defaults (inst_params inst))
      (dotimes (i 6)
        (inst_set_voice inst i (macro_voice_c (inst_params inst))))
      inst)))
